Completion Summary — 2026-07-26
# WI-2548 completion summary
## What was done
Made the two coach-bubble visual Maestro flows deterministic for release CI. The runner previously never touched system UI mode (so a light/dark visual flow inherited whatever mode the previous flow left the emulator in), and both flows polled chat-input visibility — a signal that never changes and proved nothing — instead of a real response-complete oracle. The deterministic hosted-Maestro LLM provider boundary was verified as already fully wired (apps/api/src/test-utils/maestro-e2e-worker.ts plus maestro-e2e-llm-provider.ts, entered only via the e2e CI workflow's wrangler dev entrypoint and unreachable in production, which boots src/index.ts). This completion transition was finalized on operator directive 2026-07-26 after the code landed; the on-device release-run evidence is being produced in the currently-open device window (see Caveats).
## What changed
- apps/mobile/e2e/scripts/ci-maestro-plan.mjs — flows may declare a uiMode frontmatter field, threaded through the plan's TSV/JSON output as a new third column (backwards-compatible: flows without it emit a dash).
- apps/mobile/e2e/scripts/run-ci-maestro.sh — applies the flow's requested mode via adb (cmd uimode night no/yes) immediately before that flow's app launch; flows with no declaration leave the emulator's current mode alone.
- apps/mobile/e2e/flows/learning/coach-bubble-light.yaml and coach-bubble-dark.yaml — rewritten to wait on the real assistant-response-complete testID (the chat shell's completed-assistant-response marker) and assert the exact deterministic hosted-Maestro fixture reply copy, with uiMode declared in each flow's frontmatter; indices follow the same idiom as the returning-learner resume flow. Both flows deliberately KEEP their blocked tag and PARKED header until the on-device release-run evidence lands.
## Verification
The pull request carried a full successful check set (nineteen checks including the maestro-validator, merge-completeness, API quality gate, flag-on integration, and the run-smoke suite) and a clean automated-review approval with zero findings; it was merged through the armed lane merge gate and landed on main as the squash commit recorded in Fixed In. The provider-boundary claim was verified by tracing the entrypoint split (test worker versus production index) rather than asserted.
## Caveats / Follow-ups
The fourth acceptance criterion — both flows passing on a real Android release build, then removing their blocked tags — is deliberately still open at this transition: the device window on this host is mid-session (a fresh release build containing this landed change is queued right after the WI-2600 verification leg), and the tag-removal is a small follow-up change once that evidence exists. Deferral logged here for the reviewer per the operator's 2026-07-26 finalize-now directive; the flows remain quarantined until then, so CI exposure is unchanged.
